  "id": "Compound::DB00594 - Gene::6337",
  "verbalization": "Amiloride, a drug that binds to Asic1 and Asic2, is implicated in the regulation of ligand-gated sodium channel activity, which is a key pathway leading to the participation of Scnn1a. The evidence suggests that Amiloride interacts with two distinct isoforms of Asic (Asic1 and Asic2), both of which are involved in modulating the activity of ligand-gated sodium channels. This interaction ultimately leads to the participation of Scnn1a in the channel activity, establishing a direct link between Amiloride and Scnn1a through a shared regulatory mechanism involving ligand-gated sodium channels. The integration of these pathways highlights a potential role for Amiloride in influencing the function of Scnn1a, likely through its effects on the broader sodium channel network. The evidence is consistent across multiple paths, reinforcing the notion that Amiloride acts as a modulator of Scnn1a through a common mechanism involving ligand-gated sodium channel activity.",
